# Senior Web Development Standards

- **React 19 & Next.js 15:** Use Server Components (RSC) by default. Only use `'use client'` for components with interactivity (hooks/events).
- **TypeScript:** No `any`. Use interfaces for component props. Use functional components (`const Component = ({ prop }: Props) => ...`).
- **Tailwind CSS:** Use mobile-first design. Prefer utility classes over custom CSS. Use the `cn()` utility for conditional classes.
- **Project Structure:** - Components in `src/components/`
  - Logic/Utilities in `src/lib/`
  - Page routes in `src/app/`
- **Modern UI:** - Use `lucide-react` for icons.
  - Implement "Bento Grid" layouts for the portfolio section.
  - Use `framer-motion` for subtle entrance animations.
- **Data Fetching:** For the Substack RSS feed, use a Server Component with an `async/await` fetch pattern.
- **Resume:** Maintain a structured `JSON` object for career data to keep the UI decoupled from the content.
